{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A restart between failure recording and checkpointing can misclassify a flaky post-merge check, leading defect analysis to a wrong conclusion."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A restart at the checkpoint boundary can cause the stored observation to lose its slow-regression diagnostic flag."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A confinement failure on a targeted retry is recorded as a code regression, potentially directing investigation toward the wrong cause."}]}